course: dictionary
lesson: 8353
title: Rosette: a badge, a pattern, a plant
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives you several, and the context tells you which one fits. «Leopard rosettes are small and empty in the middle» is about spots on an animal's fur, not a badge. When a word has more than one meaning, read the sentence and ask which meaning makes sense.
explain: «Winners at the show got a red rosette.» Here a rosette is a round badge made of ribbon, given as a prize. The clues are winners, show and red. Try the meaning in the sentence: "Winners got a round ribbon badge as a prize." It fits.
explain: Some words describe a shape. «A jaguar's spots are rosettes, rings with little dots inside.» Look for clue words such as rings, spots and dots to find the shape.
explain: Check your idea by swapping it into the sentence. If the meaning fits every clue, you have probably found the right one. If it does not, try the next meaning.
fact: A rosette is a round shape, often made of rings, ribbon or leaves.
fact: «Win a rosette» means to win a prize at a show or gymkhana, and the colours red, blue and yellow show the place won.
fact: «Leopard rosettes» are small and empty in the middle; «jaguar rosettes» are bigger with spots inside.
fact: Dandelions grow a rosette of leaves in a ring close to the ground.
fact: Leopards live in Africa and Asia, while jaguars live only in the Americas.
exercise: «Winners at the show each got a red rosette.» What is a rosette in this sentence? | *A round ribbon badge given as a prize | A very fast dog | A rose-shaped cake | A pond full of frogs
exercise: «A jaguar's spots are rosettes, rings with little dots inside.» What does rosette mean here? | A kind of bread | A flat stone | *A ring-shaped spot pattern on fur | A loud whisper
exercise: «Dandelions grow their leaves in a rosette near the ground.» What does rosette mean? | A red ribbon prize | *A ring of leaves growing from one point | A sudden storm | A hungry leopard
test: «Leopard rosettes are small and empty in the middle.» Where do leopards live? | *Africa and Asia | Only in the Americas | Only in Scotland | Under the sea
test: Which big cat has plain solid spots and black tear lines down its face? | Leopard | Jaguar | Dog | *Cheetah
exam: Mia says a rosette must always be a badge. Is she right? | Yes, but only for horses | No, a rosette is always a sweet | *No, a rosette can be a prize badge, an animal's spot pattern, or a ring of leaves | Yes, always
